EXT. FLOODED RICE PADDY - DAWN

Mist. Brown water to the knees. A broken dike. Frogs.

Four soldiers in a skirmish line. Slogging.

LIEUTENANT NADIA VASSILIOU (30s, helmet strap loose) in the lead. Compass in her fist.

SERGEANT FIONN MCALLISTER-DUBE (40s, radio on his back) behind her.

CORPORAL AMARA TSEGAYE (20s, rifle high, eyes wide) third.

PRIVATE LEOPOLDO "POLDO" RINCON (19, glasses taped at the hinge) last.

NADIA
(low, to the line)
Spacing. Ten feet.

They spread. Water sloshes.

POLDO
(muttering)
Ten feet. Ten feet. Ten feet.

A frog leaps. Amara jerks the rifle. Fionn grabs the barrel.

FIONN
Easy.

AMARA
Sorry.

They go on. The mist shifts.

Metal glints ahead. A crouched shape. A helmet. Then another.

Nadia raises a fist. Everyone stops.

A crack. Water jumps near Poldo.

NADIA
Down!

Nadia and Amara dive left. Fionn and Poldo dive right. A machine gun opens up, stitching the paddy.

FIONN
(shouting at the whole squad)
Stay low! Stay LOW!

Poldo lifts his head. Gets a mouthful of mud.

POLDO
(to himself)
Okay. Okay okay okay.

AMARA
(to Nadia)
Where is it?

NADIA
Treeline. Eleven o'clock.

She crawls to Fionn. He is on the radio. His lips move. Static only.

FIONN
Dead.

NADIA
Try again.

He tries. Nothing.

The firing stops. Hard silence. Frogs begin again.

Nadia peers over the dike. She stares. Her shoulders drop.

NADIA (CONT'D)
(to the squad)
Hold fire.

AMARA
Ma'am?

NADIA
Hold. Fire.

Across the paddy, the "helmets" are scarecrows. Two straw men in rusted pots. A third machine gun sits on a bamboo tripod, tied to a clapper that bangs in the breeze.

Fionn lets out a breath that turns into a laugh. Amara puts her forehead on her rifle. Poldo sits straight up out of the water, soaked to the chin.

POLDO
It's a bird scarer.

NADIA
It's a bird scarer.

She pulls her wet hat off and wrings it. Amara and Poldo stand together, shaking, and slap each other on the shoulder, hard, both laughing.

FIONN
(to Nadia)
Will you tell them she did the compass right?

NADIA
(to Fionn)
Tell them yourself. She's your lieutenant.

Fionn looks at Nadia. She looks at him. A beat, and neither can say which of them was the "she" meant.

FIONN
Aye.

They start across the paddy.
